            <title>[ZEPPELIN-2708] Should provide V scrolls for setup, usage menus in doc</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2708</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Jun Kim &amp;lt;i2r.jun@gmail.com&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
4:41 PM (2 hours ago)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; to users &lt;br/&gt;
I love it! Obviously better than before &lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/emoticons/smile.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But Usage &amp;amp; Setup drop-downs are too long and the ends of them are cut! &lt;br/&gt;
So, I think they need scroll bars like Interpreter drop-down.&lt;br/&gt;
The image below shows that the drop-down is cut.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
